# Sleigh specification for the Ricoh 2A03 (the NES/Famicom CPU) with the undocumented opcodes
# enabled, language id 6502:LE:16:2a03undoc (grm-yvmw). It is 2a03.slaspec (decimal mode
# disconnected: ADC/SBC always binary) plus the vendored undocumented-opcode semantics, whose
# own RRA/ISC/$EB add/subtract macros also honour NO_DECIMAL.
#
# Opt-in on purpose, like 6502:LE:16:undoc: with all 256 opcode bytes decodable the
# disassembler will run through data regions instead of stopping on an invalid instruction.
# ARR in 6510_illegal.sinc keeps a decimal branch; on the 2A03 that branch is compiled out
# too (see the NO_DECIMAL guard there).

@define NO_DECIMAL "1"

@include "6502core.sinc"
@include "6510_illegal.sinc"
